<article class="env-remark" id="007V">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/007V">Remark <span data-tag="007V">11.4.0.33</span>.</a> This tag was removed because the definition of $2$-category was changed. </p>
<p>Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a strictly unitary $2$-category. Then the triangle identity $(T)$ of Definition <a data-tag="007Q" href="/tag/007Q">2.2.1.1</a> can be stated more simply as the assertion that for every pair of composable $1$-morphisms $X \xrightarrow {f} Y \xrightarrow {g} Z$, the associativity constraint $\alpha _{g, \operatorname{id}_ Y, f}$ coincides with the identity map from $g \circ (\operatorname{id}_{Y} \circ f) = g \circ f = (g \circ \operatorname{id}_{Y} ) \circ f$ to itself. </p>
</article>
